      "handoff": "BUILT src/scope.mjs + src/scrub.mjs and build/tests/{scope,scrub}.test.mjs (56 new tests; 78 total, all pass).\n\nscope.mjs exports: normaliseRemote(url), gitRoot(cwd), gitRemoteUrl(cwd), gitAvailable(cwd), resolveProjectKey({cwd,env}) -> {projectKey, source, root, remote}, resolveScope({scope,cwd,env}) -> {scope, projectKey, ...}. source is one of env|git-remote|git-root|cwd|global, so mem add/doctor can show WHY a memory scoped where it did. Key order: MEM_PROJECT_KEY override > normalised remote (origin, then upstream, then first remote) > realpath of the git worktree root > realpath of cwd. Path fallbacks are absolute so they never collide with a 'host/owner/repo' remote key. Remote normalisation lowercases only the HOST (paths stay case-sensitive) and strips creds/port/.git/trailing slashes; unrecognised remotes return null and fall through to the path rather than inventing a key. All git calls are execFileSync with a 1.5s timeout, GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0, and never throw.\n\nscrub.mjs exports: RULES, findSecrets(text), isClean(text), scanFields({text,why}), assertNoSecrets(fieldsOrString,{env}) throwing SecretError (code MEM_SECRET_DETECTED, .findings). 1.2's write path should call assertNoSecrets BEFORE embedding so a rejected write costs nothing. 13 rules cover PLAN's list plus stripe/google/npm. Findings carry a masked sample ('sk-p...N chars'); hex/base64 rules are marked opaque and reveal zero characters, so nothing echoes a secret into a log. Overlapping matches are deduped by span (a JWT reports once, not also as base64).\n\nNEXT SESSION MUST KNOW\n- THE LEDGER'S VERIFY COMMAND WAS BROKEN AND I PATCHED IT. 'node --test build/tests/' does not scan the directory on this node 22.23.1 - it tries to require the path and dies with MODULE_NOT_FOUND, so it failed before running a single test. I rewrote verify to \"node --test 'build/tests/**/*.test.mjs'\" (quoted, so node globs, not bash) in all 12 todo slices that used the directory form. No other STATE.json field touched.\n- Precision tuning that is deliberate, not accidental, in scrub.mjs: the credential-assignment rule has NO leading \\b (env vars end in the keyword: OPENAI_API_KEY=, GITHUB_TOKEN=) and captures <...>/quoted values whole so '<your key>' reads as a placeholder; placeholder values (<x>, \\$VAR, ***, changeme, xxx) are allowed; exactly-40 and exactly-64 hex chars are allowed near commit/sha/hash/digest words (git SHAs are a legitimate thing to remember, other lengths are not exempt); the base64 rule needs mixed case + a digit and at most 2 slashes, which is what stops a long CamelCase file path reading as a blob.\n- MEM_ALLOW_SECRETS=1 skips the check at the assert layer only (findSecrets always reports). It exists because a rule will eventually be wrong; if you'd rather it not exist, remove it in 1.2 before anything depends on it.\n- Two of my own tests failed first run and both were real bugs, not bad tests: the placeholder gap above, and a Google-key fake of the wrong length silently falling through to the base64 rule. Keep the 'every rule has a fake sample and fires on it' test - it is what caught the second one.\n- scope tests build real throwaway git repos and skip if git is absent; they pass env:{} explicitly so an ambient MEM_PROJECT_KEY cannot green them.\n- Still not done (outside allowed working dir): the .dotfiles/.gitignore guard for 'config/claude/skills/mem/node_modules' and '*.db*'.",
