      "handoff": "BUILT src/write.mjs + `mem add` and build/tests/write.test.mjs (36 new tests; 114 total, all pass).\n\nwrite.mjs exports: KINDS, WRITABLE_STATUSES, SOURCE_KINDS, DEDUP_THRESHOLD (0.93), CONFIDENCE_BUMP (0.25), MAX_TEXT (1000) / MAX_WHY (2000), EVENT_CREATED/EVENT_MERGED, WriteError (code MEM_INVALID | MEM_DUPLICATE_UID), normaliseText, normaliseInput, bumpConfidence, mergePlan(existing,incoming) -> [{field,from,to}], nearestInScope(conn,vec,{scope,projectKey,statuses,embModel,embDim}) -> {...row, similarity} | null, recordEvent, prepareMemory, commitMemory, addMemory(input,{conn,paths,env,cwd,now,dedup,threshold,dedupStatuses}) -> {action,row,changes,similarity,nearest,eventId,scopeSource}.\n\nPipeline order is load-bearing: validate -> assertNoSecrets -> resolveScope -> embed -> one immediate transaction holding both the dedup lookup and the write (so two racing adds cannot both decide they are first). A rejected write never loads the model.\n\nDECISIONS THE NEXT SLICES INHERIT\n- TIMESTAMPS ARE EPOCH MILLISECONDS (plain Date.now()) in created_at/updated_at/expires_at. The schema does not say which; it is fixed in write.mjs and 1.3/1.5/phase-5 decay must agree.\n- Dedup scope is NARROWER than retrieval scope: scope = ? AND project_key IS ? (null-safe), never the 'global OR project' union - merging a project fact into a global one would silently widen its blast radius. Also requires matching emb_model/emb_dim (cross-vector-space distances are meaningless) and emb IS NOT NULL (a phase-5 tombstone would otherwise sort FIRST, since NULL sorts ahead of every real distance in ASC).\n- Dedup is SAME-STATUS by default (dedupStatuses defaults to [status]). A staged auto-capture must not silently bump the confidence of a memory a human already reviewed; it queues as its own staged row. Repeat captures still collapse into each other, so the review queue stays readable. Override via dedupStatuses if phase 4 wants promotion-time merging.\n- Merge policy (mergePlan, pure and unit-tested): longer text wins and the embedding travels with it; longer/absent why wins; confidence always bumps saturating toward 1 (0.5 -> 0.63 -> 0.72, never reaches 1); salience only rises when the caller passed it EXPLICITLY (normaliseInput records .explicit so a default 0.5 cannot overwrite a deliberate 0.2); pinned is sticky. A merge never demotes anything and never changes status, kind, uid, created_at or the counts.\n- add can only write status staged|active. archived/superseded are outcomes of pruning/consolidation - an add able to name them would forge a decision that was never taken.\n- Every mutation writes one memory_events row. 'merged' detail carries {similarity, threshold, changes:[{field,from,to}], previous:{updated_at}, incoming} - enough to invert without a backup. It deliberately does NOT store the old embedding blob: it stores the old TEXT, and re-embedding is 11ms. 'created' detail records the runner-up {id,similarity} that did NOT clear the threshold, which is the evidence for retuning 0.93 later.\n\nMEASURED, NOT GUESSED - 0.93 IS TIGHT\n  'always use pnpm' vs 'always use pnpm, never npm'                        0.9005  -> stays 2 rows\n  'always use pnpm to install dependencies' vs '... in this repo'          0.9301  -> merges, barely\n  'always use pnpm to install dependencies' vs '..., never npm'            0.9448  -> merges\n  'deploy with nix' vs 'deploy with nix, not docker images'                0.7630  -> stays 2 rows\nShort facts differing by a clause routinely land at 0.90 and do NOT merge. Two of my tests failed first run purely because I assumed a pair was a duplicate and it was not - measure the pair before asserting on it. The test file pins these strings as PNPM / PNPM_LONGER / UNRELATED constants with the numbers in a comment; reuse them. Do not pick 0.9301-class pairs for tests, they sit on the knife edge.\n\nCLI: mem add <text...> [--why --kind --global|--project --pin --staged --salience --confidence --expires-in <days> --source --session --threshold --no-dedup --cwd --json]. Loose positional words are joined with spaces so quoting is optional, and unknown --flags are REJECTED rather than folded into the memory text (silently storing '--whi typo' as part of a fact is exactly the corruption a memory store must not have). Exit 2 (not 1) on MEM_SECRET_DETECTED so a hook can tell 'you gave me a secret' from 'mem is broken'. --json strips emb (1.5KB of float noise).\n\nTESTING NOTE FOR 1.3/1.4: the CLI tests get real isolation by pointing CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA at a temp dir and SYMLINKING node_modules + models in from the real data dir - no download, no npm, own database. Copy that pattern; overriding only dbPath does not work for a subprocess.\n\nKept MEM_ALLOW_SECRETS=1 (1.1 offered to remove it). It is now depended on by nothing except assertNoSecrets itself; the write path passes env straight through.\n\nStill not done (outside allowed working dir): the .dotfiles/.gitignore guard for 'config/claude/skills/mem/node_modules' and '*.db*'.",
