      "goal": "src/search.mjs implementing the 7 steps in PLAN.md: scoped candidates, vector leg (LIMIT 20), lexical leg via fts_match, RRF fusion at k=60, strength boost, threshold gate, cap 5. Returns [] when nothing clears the gate. `mem search <query>` with --json.",
      "verify": "node --test 'build/tests/**/*.test.mjs'",
      "status": "done",
      "handoff": "BUILT src/search.mjs + `mem search` + build/tests/search.test.mjs (44 new tests; 158 total, all pass). Cold-process search at 200 rows: ~310ms (phase-1 exit budget is 400ms).\n\nsearch.mjs exports: VECTOR_LIMIT/LEXICAL_LIMIT (20), RRF_K (60), MAX_RESULTS (5), VECTOR_THRESHOLD (0.35), LEXICAL_GATE_COVERAGE (0.6), STRENGTH_WEIGHT (0.3), PINNED_WEIGHT (0.2), HALFLIFE_H0 (30), HALFLIFE_ALPHA (0.6), DAY_MS, MAX_TERMS (12), STOPWORDS, tokenise, queryTerms, halflifeDays, retention, strength, boostFactor, fuse, rankLexical, countCandidates, vectorLeg, lexicalLeg, searchScoped(conn,vector,terms,opts) -> {results,stats}, searchDetail(query,opts) -> {query,terms,results,stats}, search(query,opts) -> Result[].\n\nMEASURED fts_match IN THIS TURSO BUILD — it is NOT SQLite FTS5, do not assume FTS5 semantics anywhere later:\n  fts_match(text,'a b')  pure OR across terms, never AND\n  operators              none — AND/OR/NOT are matched as ordinary terms\n  quoted phrases         not honoured ('\"dependencies install\"' matched reversed text)\n  'depend*'              no match — no prefix, no stemming, no substring\n  tokenizer              splits on EVERY non-alphanumeric (MEM_PROJECT_KEY -> mem|project|key,\n                         pnpm-lock.yaml -> pnpm|lock|yaml, don't -> don|t) but NOT camelCase\n                         (getUserById stays one token; 'user' does not match it)\n  case                   insensitive\n  fts_score(text)        returns 0 — scoring index is feature-gated off\nTwo consequences: (a) a raw prompt must be tokenised+stopworded before it reaches fts_match or it matches everything containing 'the'/'use'; (b) the lexical leg CANNOT be ranked in SQL, so SQL only prunes and JS ranks.\n\nDEVIATION FROM PLAN, deliberate: PLAN says lexical leg 'LIMIT 20' in SQL. There is nothing to ORDER BY (fts_score dead), so a SQL LIMIT would return an arbitrary 20 in rowid order — the 20 oldest. The fetch is unbounded and the cap is applied after JS ranking. This is also load-bearing for correctness: document frequencies are counted from the full match set, and because fts_match is pure OR that set provably contains every candidate holding a term, making the df exact rather than sampled. Affordable because it pulls text while the vector leg beside it already reads the 1.5KB embedding of every candidate.\n\nDECISIONS THE NEXT SLICES INHERIT\n- Lexical score = IDF COVERAGE: of the total idf mass of the query's terms, the fraction this row accounts for. idf = ln(1 + N/(1+df)). This is what makes 'exact lexical hit' meaningful under OR semantics — one shared common word scores ~0.15 and cannot clear the 0.6 gate, while a lone rare identifier scores ~1.0. The lexical leg exists for identifiers (MEM_PROJECT_KEY, pnpm-lock.yaml) because that is what the embedding model represents worst.\n- THE GATE IS A DISJUNCTION: sim >= 0.35 OR coverage >= 0.6. One of my tests failed first run because I assumed raising --threshold alone would empty the results; it did not, the row cleared lexically. Tighten both legs to close it. Gate runs BEFORE the cap, so five weak items cannot hide a sixth that cleared.\n- DECAY IS APPLIED ONCE. PLAN step 5 says '× (1+0.3·salience+0.2·pinned) × recency_decay' but the decay section supersedes it ('strength replaces raw salience in the retrieval boost'). retention already lives inside strength; multiplying recency in again would square the decay. boostFactor = 1 + 0.3·strength + 0.2·pinned. Verified halflifeDays(5)=87.9 matches PLAN's '≈87'.\n- An unused memory decays from updated_at (last_used_at -> updated_at -> created_at), else 'never used' and 'used a moment ago' score identically.\n- EXPIRY IS ENFORCED AT READ TIME, not in PLAN's step 1: '(expires_at IS NULL OR expires_at > ?)' is in the candidate WHERE. TTL expiry is a scheduled tier-1 job, and between two runs an expired row is still status='active'; injecting a fact the user gave a lifetime to is an error nobody notices. Phase 5a should still archive them, this is just the guard in between.\n- Vector leg skips emb IS NULL and mismatched emb_model/emb_dim, same reasoning as write.mjs. Consequence: after a model change retrieval silently returns nothing until re-embed. A lexical-only row (tombstone, or outside the vector top-20) gets similarity: null and can still pass the gate on coverage.\n- Sequential, not Promise.all, for the two legs — one connection, interleaved statements are not a guarantee this driver makes.\n- search() returns [] and `mem search` EXITS 0 when nothing clears the gate. A hook asks on every prompt; nothing-matched is the designed answer, not a failure.\n\nSCHEMA CONFLICT FOR PHASE 5 (found, not fixed — outside this slice): PLAN's pruning ladder rung 3 tombstones with 'emb = NULL', but schema v1 declares 'emb BLOB NOT NULL'. Tombstoning needs a migration (v2 table rebuild) before it can run. search.mjs already tolerates NULL embs.\n\nTUNING EVIDENCE FOR PHASE 3 (measured query->memory cosines, real model):\n  'how do I install dependencies?'  vs 'always use pnpm to install dependencies'  0.534\n  'what do we use for testing?'     vs 'prefer Vitest over Jest for unit tests'   0.430\n  'which package manager should I use?' vs the pnpm memory                        0.387  <- near the gate\n  'how is the app deployed?'        vs 'deploy with nix flakes, not docker'       0.212  <- MISSED, and\n      lexical cannot rescue it either: no stemming, so 'deployed' != 'deploy'. This is the honest\n      cost of 0.35 and the clearest thing for the phase-3 harness to weigh.\n  any unrelated prompt (France, otters) vs anything                              < 0.15\nJunk is rejected by a wide margin, so 'inject nothing on an unrelated prompt' holds comfortably; the risk at 0.35 is false negatives, not false positives. Do not use 0.387-class pairs as test fixtures.\n\nSTILL NOT DONE (outside allowed working dir, inherited from 1.1/1.2): the .dotfiles/.gitignore guard for 'config/claude/skills/mem/node_modules' and '*.db*'.",
